<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Province of West Florida</h1><p class="st-meta">1763 CE – 1783 CE · capital Pensacola</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A British Gulf Coast colony stretching from Pensacola to the Mississippi, lost to Spanish forces during the American Revolution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-proclamation-of-1763">Royal Proclamation of 1763</a> from territory <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> gained under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1763">Treaty of Paris</a>: the western part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-florida">Spanish Florida</a> plus French lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> around Mobile. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pensacola">Pensacola</a> became the capital, and in 1764 the northern boundary was pushed up to the latitude of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazoo-river">Yazoo River</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> had an elected assembly alongside royal governors such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-johnstone">George Johnstone</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-chester">Peter Chester</a>. Settlers came from the older colonies and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> to farm along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natchez-chiefdom">Natchez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baton-rouge">Baton Rouge</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pensacola">Pensacola</a> and Mobile lived on the deerskin trade with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/muscogee-confederacy">Muscogee Confederacy</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/choctaw-nation">Choctaw Nation</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chickasaw-nation">Chickasaw Nation</a>. Like <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-east-florida">East Florida</a>, it stayed loyal to the Crown after 1776.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> entered the war in 1779, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-de-galvez">Bernardo de Gálvez</a>, governor of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-louisiana">Spanish Louisiana</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baton-rouge">Baton Rouge</a>, Mobile and finally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pensacola">Pensacola</a> in 1781. The 1783 peace confirmed Spanish possession; disputes over the region's border later fed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-west-florida">Republic of West Florida</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/province-of-west-florida.jpg" alt="Province of West Florida" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Wangi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_ensign_of_Great_Britain_(1707%E2%80%931800).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1763 CE – 1783 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pensacola</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>George Johnstone, Peter Chester</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>West Florida</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1773&amp;focus=province-of-west-florida" aria-label="Province of West Florida on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2418 1068 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Province of West Florida lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2738 1324L4997 651M2738 1324L4909 989M2738 1324L2886 1342"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M4909 989h0M2886 1342h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2738 1324h0"/><pat